+    /**
+     * Whether the entity is a registered ExcelSummons summon of CAST origin —
+     * an entity a Magic cast actually conjured, as opposed to an ADOPTED
+     * registration (a player's own hand-tamed pet that ExcelSummons' sweep
+     * merely registered). The distinction is ExcelSummons' own record
+     * ({@code ExcelSummonsAPI.getRecord(Entity)} → {@code SummonRecord.origin()},
+     * an enum with exactly the constants CAST and ADOPTED since ExcelSummons
+     * 0.1.4); it is the same origin its rank cap and dismiss rules read.
+     *
+     * <p>Mike's ruling (Nov 15, 2026): a cast summon fighting as a pet earns
+     * its owner no Taming XP, but an adopted pet still does. This check is
+     * therefore deliberately narrower than {@link #isSummon}: it answers true
+     * ONLY on a positive CAST identification. An unregistered entity, an
+     * ADOPTED registration, a record whose origin reads as anything else, an
+     * absent plugin, or any probe failure all answer false — the pet pays
+     * normally. ExcelSummons' own defaults lean the same way: a stored record
+     * with no origin restores as ADOPTED there, so legacy registrations pay.
+     *
+     * @param entity the entity to check, may be null
+     * @return true only when ExcelSummons is present and its record for the
+     *         entity positively reports CAST origin; false in every other case
+     */
+    public static boolean isCastSummon(@Nullable Entity entity) {
+        if (entity == null || !pluginEnabled(EXCEL_SUMMONS_PLUGIN)) {
+            return false;
+        }
+
+        final Method method = resolveSummonsRecordMethod();
+        if (method == null) {
+            return false;
+        }
+
+        try {
+            final Object record = method.invoke(null, entity);
+            if (record == null) {
+                // Not registered at all: not positively a cast summon.
+                return false;
+            }
+
+            // origin() and name() are resolved from the live objects on every
+            // call, so a record produced by a reloaded classloader is read
+            // through its own classes, never a cached foreign handle.
+            final Method originMethod = record.getClass().getMethod("origin");
+            final Object origin = originMethod.invoke(record);
+            if (origin == null) {
+                return false;
+            }
+
+            final Method nameMethod = origin.getClass().getMethod("name");
+            final Object name = nameMethod.invoke(origin);
